WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.294 --> 00:00:19.760
When Nina arrived at summer camp, Mr.

2
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.621
Dunn was setting a basket of lemons on the picnic table.

3
00:00:22.641 --> 00:00:24.562
"Good morning, Mr.

4
00:00:24.582 --> 00:00:25.942
Dunn!" she called.

5
00:00:25.962 --> 00:00:28.684
"Good morning, Nina," Mr.

6
00:00:28.724 --> 00:00:29.324
Dunn said.

7
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:33.141
Nina picked three lemons out of the basket.

8
00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.602
Her aunt had tried to teach her how to juggle last week.

9
00:00:41.683 --> 00:00:43.244
But Nina still couldn't do it.

10
00:00:44.124 --> 00:00:45.864
Plop, plop, plop.

11
00:00:46.785 --> 00:00:48.445
The lemons landed on the ground.

12
00:00:49.485 --> 00:00:51.446
By now the other campers arrived.

13
00:00:55.347 --> 00:00:57.748
Nina!" Bobby laughed.

14
00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.001
"Did you sign up for clown school?"

15
00:01:02.022 --> 00:01:03.102
Nina frowned at him.

16
00:01:03.122 --> 00:01:05.043
"I'm not a clown!"

17
00:01:06.103 --> 00:01:07.304
Izzie picked up the lemons.

18
00:01:07.324 --> 00:01:10.025
"Do we need these lemons today?"

19
00:01:11.546 --> 00:01:12.667
Mr. Dunn nodded.

20
00:01:12.687 --> 00:01:15.168
"It's okay that they fell.

21
00:01:16.188 --> 00:01:19.330
We're going to squeeze all of the juice out of them anyway."

22
00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:23.071
"Yay! We're making lemonade!"

23
00:01:23.492 --> 00:01:24.192
Izzie cried.

24
00:01:28.136 --> 00:01:30.717
Inside the gym the kids gathered around Mr.

25
00:01:30.737 --> 00:01:36.520
Dunn. "Lemonade is one of my favorite summer drinks," the teacher said.

26
00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.781
"It's one of mine too!"

27
00:01:39.161 --> 00:01:39.781
said Izzie.

28
00:01:39.801 --> 00:01:42.302
"I like it really sweet."

29
00:01:43.443 --> 00:01:46.204
"Then you'll love this recipe," Mr.

30
00:01:46.264 --> 00:01:46.904
Dunn said.

31
00:01:48.325 --> 00:01:49.485
Ethan read the board.

32
00:01:49.505 --> 00:01:54.928
"To make the syrup, we have to heat the sugar and water until the sugar dissolves.

33
00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:58.238
But how will we know when the sugar dissolves?"

34
00:01:58.258 --> 00:02:01.441
"It'll disappear," said Mr.

35
00:02:01.481 --> 00:02:06.685
Dunn. "And turn into a clear syrup."

36
00:02:07.066 --> 00:02:08.827
Ethan and Jason made the syrup.

37
00:02:14.492 --> 00:02:16.034
The other campers cut lemons.

38
00:02:17.255 --> 00:02:19.717
Mr. Dunn handed forks to the lemon-cutters.

39
00:02:19.737 --> 00:02:22.860
"Now we remove the seeds."

40
00:02:24.324 --> 00:02:29.528
After Nina, Izzie, and Bobby removed the seeds, they squeezed the lemons to make juice.

41
00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:34.651
we take out the pulp?"

42
00:02:35.091 --> 00:02:35.932
Nina asked.

43
00:02:35.952 --> 00:02:38.053
"No way!"

44
00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:39.194
Izzie cried.

45
00:02:39.214 --> 00:02:41.936
"Pulpy lemonade is the best!"

46
00:02:46.379 --> 00:02:49.441
Soon the syrup was cool, and the lemon juice was ready.

47
00:02:51.702 --> 00:02:53.684
Bobby poured them both into the pitcher.

48
00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:58.121
"Is that it?"

49
00:02:58.441 --> 00:02:59.061
he asked.

50
00:03:00.202 --> 00:03:01.423
"Almost," Mr.

51
00:03:01.463 --> 00:03:02.103
Dunn said.

52
00:03:02.123 --> 00:03:04.484
"We made the sweet part.

53
00:03:05.725 --> 00:03:07.206
And we made the sour part.

54
00:03:08.347 --> 00:03:10.048
Now we have to add water."

55
00:03:10.068 --> 00:03:12.489
"How much water?"

56
00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:13.690
Nina asked.

57
00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:17.252
"Let's start by adding two and half cups.

58
00:03:18.453 --> 00:03:22.695
We'll keep tasting the lemonade until it's just right," Mr.

59
00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:23.356
Dunn said.

60
00:03:24.312 --> 00:03:27.234
They each poured half a cup of water into the pitcher.

61
00:03:33.697 --> 00:03:35.578
Izzie poured herself a little lemonade.

62
00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:39.981
It's sweet!"

63
00:03:41.061 --> 00:03:42.482
Nina tried a small sip.

64
00:03:42.502 --> 00:03:44.804
"It's too sweet!

65
00:03:45.564 --> 00:03:46.785
Let's add more water."

66
00:03:48.346 --> 00:03:52.348
After they added one more half cup of water, Bobby tried the lemonade.

67
00:03:54.704 --> 00:03:56.485
"Mmm! That's good."

68
00:03:57.546 --> 00:03:58.906
Ethan tasted some too.

69
00:03:58.926 --> 00:04:01.188
"I think it needs more water.

70
00:04:02.088 --> 00:04:03.008
But only a little bit."

71
00:04:03.028 --> 00:04:05.890
"I agree," said Jason.

72
00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:10.092
"Let's just add ice cubes now," Nina suggested.

73
00:04:10.112 --> 00:04:12.573
"Great idea!"

74
00:04:12.973 --> 00:04:13.553
said Mr.

75
00:04:13.593 --> 00:04:19.196
Dunn. "Ice will cool the lemonade and add just a tiny bit of water."

76
00:04:24.064 --> 00:04:27.225
He got ice cubes from a cooler and added them to the pitcher.

77
00:04:31.026 --> 00:04:33.387
Then everyone had a glass of iced lemonade.

78
00:04:33.407 --> 00:04:39.548
"Wow! This is better than the lemonade at the deli," Izzie said.

79
00:04:39.568 --> 00:04:42.489
"This is good enough to sell!"

80
00:04:42.749 --> 00:04:43.469
Bobby said.

81
00:04:43.489 --> 00:04:47.191
"We could have a Kids Central Lemonade Stand!"

82
00:04:47.611 --> 00:04:48.431
Nina cried.

83
00:04:48.451 --> 00:04:53.899
"Then instead of juggling lemons, I can make lemonade!"
